GNU libiconv, and what it obliges
---------------------------------

GNU libiconv is LGPL. This repository does not redistribute it: it is fetched
and built inside the build environment by internal/envx/libiconv.go, and no
copy is committed here.

pgb links it STATICALLY into any binary it builds that calls iconv. The LGPL's
relinking obligation therefore attaches to those binaries, not to this
repository. Anyone shipping pgb output should check that against their own
requirements.

`pg-toolkit binary build --no-iconv` produces a binary with no libiconv in it and no such
obligation, at the cost of the gconv failures docs/design/iconv.md describes.
